# The second registered queue, and the one drop path nothing else reaches.
#
# `fifo` is compiled into both halves of the gate and no other scenario uses it; and every
# other scenario drains before it closes, so `DropReason::Closed` -- the path where the two
# planes are structurally DIFFERENT (Python reads what `close()` returns, C++ routes through
# `on_drop_`) -- was in the vocabulary and in no golden.
scenario fifo_close_drains
records_min 14

queue fifo
capacity 3
overflow drop_oldest
max_batch_size 1
max_delay_us 0

put cam_a
put cam_b
put cam_c
# Full: fifo drops the OLDEST, which is the whole difference from `fair`.
put cam_d
# One item out, three still queued when the close comes -- so the drain order is compared
# too, not just the reason.
take
close
